Dave Airlie wrote:
> does this help?
>
> I'm not sure why your GPU isn't using GSP instead of ACR but this should fix it.
>
> Dave.
>
> On Wed, 30 Sept 2026 at 07:53, Woody Suwalski <terraluna977@gmail.com> wrote:
>> Hello, I have noticed a kernel crash in 7.3-rc5. I am quite sure it was
>> not in 7.3-rc4. (nor 7.2.8)
>>
>> The side effect is that system would hang trying to do suspend to ram.
>>
>> Is it something you are already aware of? Any patches to try?
>> Or do I need to set up bisecting for this issue?
>>
>> Thanks, Woody
>>
>> terraluna977@gmail.com
Thanks for the patch.

Dave's patch seems to work OK. Tested with the rebuilt nouveau.ko.

I have noticed a new message in dmesg:
[   24.236944] [   T3392] nouveau 0000:01:00.0: fb: VPR locked, but no 
scrubber binary!

Thanks, Woody

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nvkm/engine/device/user.c 
b/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nvkm/engine/device/user.c
index f78e6b9b4292..b841d66f8bb3 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nvkm/engine/device/user.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nvkm/engine/device/user.c
@@ -201,7 +201,7 @@ nvkm_udevice_gcx_ready(struct nvkm_udevice *udev, 
void *data, u32 size)
      } *args = data;
      int ret = -ENOSYS;

-    if (!gsp) {
+    if (!gsp || !gsp->rm) {
          args->v0.ready = NV_DEVICE_GC6_READY | NV_DEVICE_GCOFF_READY;
          return 0;
      }


